<Concept title="Autopilot reliability" section="Engineering">
  <p>The autopilot MUST collect quest items on the first visit to an ordinary transit
    room after clearing its enemies. It MUST NOT schedule a later detour solely for
    that collection. Gate, switch, dialog and NPC dependencies MUST retain their
    scheduled visits. Terminal and section-transition cells MUST retain their role.</p>
  <p>Counter NPC and warp-pad interactions MUST observe the expected overlay after
    each press. If absent after two seconds, retry up to three total attempts, then
    fail with the player position and nearest interactable. Observing the expected
    overlay MUST cancel retries even if it closes before the deadline. Scene changes
    MUST cancel obsolete attempts. Negative menu-input probes expecting no interaction
    are exempt.</p>
  <p>These are test-infrastructure rules, not claims about original PSZ behavior.
    Original gate/key dependencies remain governed by /states/field-gates and psz-re
    evidence. Grades remain unchanged pending owner playtesting.</p>
</Concept>
